  "term": "sexual arousal",
  "definition": "Sexual arousal is the body’s physical state of activation in response to sexual contact or other erotic stimulation. It involves signals traveling through the central nervous system along with bodily changes such as sex hormone release, increased blood flow to the genitals, and reduced nerve-driven narrowing of blood vessels in that area.",
